  "body": "Callback interface objects already have a \"name\" property (when exposed due to the presence of constants) . The omission of a \"length\" prop (with value `0`) in the spec seems more accidental than deliberate. Chrome, Safari and Firefox all implement it, e.g.:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nNodeFilter.length;\r\n// => 0\r\n```",
